---
functor: 1
title: File and front matter
---

set heading(numbering: none)

A Functor file is plain text with the extension `.fn`. It has front matter, then declarations, then the text.

# Front matter

The front matter is between two lines of `---` at the top of the file.

```fn
---
functor: 1
title: Notes on fields
author: E, A. N. Other
date: 25 November 2026
---
```

| Setting | Meaning |
|:--|:--|
| `functor` | The language version. Write `functor: 1`. Without it, the compiler gives a warning. |
| `title` | The title of the document. |
| `author` or `authors` | One or more names, with commas between them. |
| `date` | Any text. |

The compiler ignores an unknown setting and gives a warning with a hint.

# Order of the file

1. Front matter.
2. Declarations: `object`, `sym`, `let`, `set`. Each one is on its own line. A declaration works from its line to the end of the file.
3. Text: headings, paragraphs, math, blocks.

# Versions

A file states its language version. When the language changes in a way that breaks old files, the version number goes up, and `functor migrate` will update old files. The canonical names change only with a new version.

# Commands

| Command | Result |
|:--|:--|
| `functor check file.fn` | Each problem as `file:line:col: error: message`, with a hint |
| `functor compile file.fn` | An HTML file |
| `functor pdf file.fn` | A PDF file that Functor sets itself |
| `functor glyph theta.hat` | The SVG of one recipe |
| `functor trace file.fn 12:5` | The four layers of each symbol: meaning, style, construction, glyph. The line and column are optional. See [Notation check and trace](help/notation.html). |
